  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Return and Reintegration Management and Addressing Irregular Migration in Lebanon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In recent years, Lebanon has experienced a sharp decline in its economic, political, and security conditions, resulting in a rise in irregular migration to Europe. This ongoing trend puts pressure on destination countries&apos; migration management and asylum systems. To tackle this issue, they have implemented various measures, including voluntary and forced return programmes. Recognizing that the success of these programmes relies on the cooperation of origin countries, this project will seek to support a system that facilitates the voluntary return, readmission, and sustainable reintegration of Lebanese irregular migrants. The project will also focus on addressing the socioeconomic factors that drive Lebanese individuals to migrate irregularly to Europe and attempt re-migration.</narrative>
  </description>
